# Claude Code local state
# `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/` so a single file can be un-ignored below — git will
# not resurrect a path inside an excluded DIRECTORY, so the trailing-slash form makes the
# negation on the next line silently do nothing.
.claude/*
# The one exception: project-scoped hooks belong to the repo, not the machine. Everything
# else in here (settings.local.json's permission allowlist, scheduled_tasks.lock) is
# session or machine state and stays ignored.
!.claude/settings.json

# V1.50.A — cycle27-surface fixture's SwiftPM-resolved checkouts
fixtures/cycle27-surface/.build/
fixtures/cycle27-surface/Package.resolved

# The integer-division-generator fixture's build products. Unlike the fixtures
# above it resolves nothing over the network (the standard library is its
# subject), so there is no Package.resolved to ignore.
fixtures/integer-division-generator/.build/

# SwiftLint config backups left by the SwiftLintRuleStudio editor on save
.swiftlint.yml.*.backup

# Verify-pipeline synthesized SwiftPM workdirs (build artifacts; index.json
# stays tracked). Matches any `.swiftinfer/verify-workdir/` — the fixture's
# and any incidental one at the repo root from a dev `swift-infer verify` run.
**/.swiftinfer/verify-workdir/

# Python bytecode cache from the swift.org study scripts (scripts/ is study
# tooling, not product code — the .py sources are tracked, the cache is not).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Calibration triage decision files — regenerable per-cycle scratch produced
# by `discover-interaction --interactive` / the cycle re-triage. The durable
# record is the cycle-N findings doc worksheet + calibration-cycle-N-data/.
**/.swiftinfer/interaction-decisions.json

# The verify-refutability experiment's generated artifacts. `index.json` is regenerable with
# `swift-infer index --target VerifyRefutability`, and the measured RESULTS are recorded in
# `predictions.json` alongside the frozen predictions — which is the file that matters.
fixtures/verify-refutability/.swiftinfer/

# Toolchain driver artifacts (`scripts/toolchain.sh`). Written into whatever target the
# driver is pointed at, which includes this repo's own fixtures. `run.json` is the useful
# one — it makes two runs comparable — but it records a moment, not a decision, so it is
# regenerated rather than tracked.
**/.toolchain-run/

# This repo's OWN generated `.swiftinfer/`, at the root only — `**/` would be wrong, since
# `fixtures/cycle27-surface/.swiftinfer/index.json` is tracked deliberately as a frozen corpus.
#
# The decisive argument is not "it is regenerable" (it is — `reindexIfNeeded` rebuilds it on a
# stale read) but that `index.json` stores **absolute paths including the username**: the tracked
# fixture index reads `/Users/joecursio/…` and a local one reads `/Users/josephcursio/…`. Tracking
# it would conflict on every sync between the two machines and be wrong on whichever pulled last.
#
# `verify-evidence.json` and `kit-evidence.json` are per-run records with wall-clock stamps.
#
# `verify-corpus.json` is the one with a real claim to being tracked — it is the durable replay
# corpus, and it only works as a *permanent* regression guard if it is committed. It is ignored
# here rather than tracked because every local verify run appends to it, so tracking it trades
# git-status noise for commit churn. That trade is a decision worth making explicitly; until then
# `git add -f .swiftinfer/verify-corpus.json` is how to take it.
/.swiftinfer/
